<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Pemex reports Feb average crude exports.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Pemex reports Feb average crude exports.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's state oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) said on Friday it exported an average 1.567 million barrels per day (bpd) of crude in February.</p>
<p>This figure compares with Pemex's February 1996 average exports of 1.505 million bpd.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of crudes by type and destination:</p>
<p>  Maya exports			     853,500 bpd</p>
<p>    To North America		     739,500 bpd</p>
<p>    To Europe				114,000 bpd</p>
<p>    To Far East				    0 bpd</p>
<p>  Isthmus exports			  180,000 bpd</p>
<p>    To North America		     109,000 bpd</p>
<p>    To Europe				  6,000 bpd</p>
<p>    To Far East			     65,000 bpd</p>
<p>  Olmeca exports			   533,000 bpd</p>
<p>    To North America		     533,000 bpd</p>
<p>Geographical Distribution</p>
<p>    North America				 88 pct</p>
<p>    Europe					   8 pct</p>
<p>    Far East					 4 pct</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903. E-mail at timna.tanners@reuters.com))</p>
